    "style": "Streamline Moderne",
    "year_built_as_surveyed": "1946",
    "note": "A Streamline Moderne multi-family residence of 1946 in the Mission — a district the statement says has few of them. Postwar, but still a good example of the style: a flat roof with coping, stucco cladding, rounded corners and curved surfaces, curved railings, porthole windows, continuous windows at the building corners, a vestibule entrance and glass blocks. Eligible as a district contributor, though the statement judges it would need a more exuberant display to qualify individually."
